Modifications by the LazyClaw project:

  - brain.py: added `claude_cli` provider that routes through LazyClaw's
    `lazyclaw.llm.providers.claude_cli_provider.ClaudeCLIProvider` so
    requests run on the user's Claude Max subscription via the `claude -p`
    binary (zero per-call API cost) instead of the paid Anthropic API.

  - brain.py: model registry bumped from claude-opus-4-6 to claude-opus-4-7;
    claude-sonnet-4-6 added to the priority list.

  - pyproject.toml + claude_bug_bounty/__init__.py added so the project is
    pip-installable as `claude_bug_bounty`. This enables in-process
    integration from LazyClaw's skill bundle (no subprocess overhead, shared
    audit log + DB transactions).

All upstream commands, skills, agents, scope_checker, AutopilotGuard,
validate (7-Question Gate), CVSS 4.0 scoring, and 280 unit tests preserved
unchanged.
